# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Downloaded / cached market data (regenerable via bootstrap.py + auto-fetch)
mf_cache/

# Local tooling
.claude/

# Secrets. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is the only key this system takes, and it is read from
# the environment (mf_datasources.py) — never committed, never defaulted in code.
# But the setup path literally tells you to "paste key in .env" (mf_datasources.py's
# health table) and to `export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...` (bootstrap.py), and an
# untracked .env is one `git add -A` away from being a committed one. That was a
# private-repo footgun; in a PUBLIC repo it is a published key. Ignore it explicitly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
